{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1498155204,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxMDQ1OTc2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1601#issuecomment-310459760"},"message":"I think supporting hierarchical would be useful, but at the same time also tricky. I would be able to set a \"tag\" for all files in a subtree. At the same time, I would not be able to use such a tag to move data via annex.\n\nI find it difficult to map triples onto annex' meta data capabilties. Hence in #1589 I went for unification with annex (except for key definitions). I think this works well. Provides a meaningful, yet minimal metadata system that complements \"bigger\", but separate metadata sets.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1503994290,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTIyNTEzMDAwMw=="},"status":2}]}